# Employee & Department Salary Analysis — SQL

## Project Overview

This project uses MySQL to analyze employee and department data, with a focus on employee headcount, department-wise salary analysis, salary expenses, employee rankings, and salary comparisons.

## Business Objectives

The analysis was performed to understand:

- Total number of employees
- Employee count by department
- Average salary by department
- Highest and lowest salary by department
- Total salary expense by department
- Employees with salaries above their department average
- Highest-paid employees
- Top employees within each department
- Departments with the highest average salary
- Departments with the highest total salary expense

## Analysis Performed

The project contains 15 SQL analysis questions covering:

1. Total employee count
2. Employee count by department
3. Average salary by department
4. Highest salary by department
5. Lowest salary by department
6. Total salary expense by department
7. Department salary expense and average salary
8. Departments above the overall average salary
9. Top 3 highest-paid employees
10. Top 3 employees in each department
11. Employee salary compared with department average
12. Employees earning above their department average
13. Department with the highest average salary
14. Department with the highest total salary expense
15. Top 5 employees earning above their department average

